/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The construction industry significantly contributes to air pollution globally, leading to substantial fines and regulatory actions. For instance, in 2024, authorities in Delhi, India, fined the owners of nearly over 7,500 construction sites for violating pollution regulations. The Central Pollution Control Board \(CPCB\) rated the air quality in New Delhi as 'very poor,' with a score of 373 on their index. Environmental compensation was levied on almost 600 construction sites, and 56 of them were closed)
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
